    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d590-a4">

                <pb facs="0953" n="817" xml:id="pg817"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign office to colonial office.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-06-21"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 21,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your letter of the 29th
                    instant, I am directed by the Marquis of Salisbury to convey to you his
                    concurrence in the dispatch to the governor of Newfoundland respecting the limit
                    of French fishery rights on the west coast of that island, of which a draught
                    was therein inclosed.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
